import <wdoc.wcl>

concept why_use_wskill {
  name = "Why use this?"
  summary = "Preserve a topic's knowledge in a reusable format that serves both people and AI agents — and still works manually if you lose access to the agent."
  related = [wskill_concept, selfcontained]
  body {
    p <<DOC
      The reason to use a wskill is to preserve knowledge in a reusable format. This matters
      more as work shifts to AI: knowledge that lives only in someone's head, or only inside a
      model, is easily lost. Capturing a topic once as self-contained data keeps it durable,
      shareable, and easy to keep current.
    DOC

    p <<DOC
      The key idea is we have one source that can be used for multiple uses. A reference for the
      topic, an AI Skill and also a training resource on the topic.
    DOC
    p ""
  }
}
